<script>
import LastTouched from 'crm/src/activity/lib/LastTouched.abide'
import lastTouchedSource from 'crm/src/activity/lib/LastTouched.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import lastTouchedTestSource from 'crm/src/activity/lib/LastTouched.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import DealFigures from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealFigures.abide'
import dealFiguresSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealFigures.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import dealFiguresBenchSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealFigures.bench.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import dealFiguresTestSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealFigures.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
import Snippet from '#src/lib/Snippet.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="Money, percents and counts in a column, with a dash for what is missing">
        <Example
            id="format-figures"
            title="`format.money`, `format.percent`, `format.plural` — figures as words"
            summary="The open deals, each with its amount and its chance of closing, and a tile weighing them up. Add a lead that has no amount yet."
            files={{
                'src/deals/lib/DealFigures.abide': dealFiguresSource,
                'src/deals/lib/DealFigures.test.ts': dealFiguresTestSource,
                'src/deals/lib/DealFigures.bench.ts': dealFiguresBenchSource,
            }}
        >
            <DealFigures />
        </Example>

        <p>The bench writes every row's amount and chance for a pipeline of 100 deals, and of 1,000.
            Its ratio is what a column costs as it grows: each formatter is built once for a set of
            options and kept, so a row pays for the writing and never for the building.</p>

        <p>Import <code>format</code> from <code>@abide/abide</code> and call a formatter in the
            slot. Each takes <code>unknown</code>, so a column drops in as it is: a
            <code>null</code>, a <code>NaN</code> or a string it cannot read is written as an em
            dash rather than as <code>$NaN</code>.</p>

        <Snippet source={dealFiguresSource} path="src/deals/lib/DealFigures.abide" from={['{#for deal of deals']} />

        <p>Every formatter writes <code>en-US</code> unless you pass a <code>locale</code>, on the
            server and in the browser alike. A page rendered on the server reads the same once the
            browser takes it over, which the visitor's own locale would not promise.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>You write</th><th>It reads</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>{'format.money(12500)'}</code></td><td>$12,500.00</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{'format.money(1_250_000, { compact: true })'}</code></td><td>$1.3M</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{'format.percent(0.125)'}</code></td><td>12.5%</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{'format.number(1200)'}</code></td><td>1,200</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{"format.plural(2, 'company', 'companies')"}</code></td><td>2 companies</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{"format.list(['Ada', 'Grace', 'Alan'])"}</code></td><td>Ada, Grace, and Alan</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{'format.bytes(1_500_000)'}</code></td><td>1.5 MB</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p><code>digits</code> fixes the digits after the point. <code>signed</code> puts a
            <code>+</code> on a positive change, and <code>currency</code> names the currency an
            amount is in.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Dates and how long ago, in a fixed time zone">
        <Example
            id="format-time"
            title="`format.relative`, `format.date` — a time as words"
            summary="The last touch with each contact, and when it was. Log a call and the new touch reads now, with the exact time on hover."
            files={{
                'src/activity/lib/LastTouched.abide': lastTouchedSource,
                'src/activity/lib/LastTouched.test.ts': lastTouchedTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <LastTouched />
        </Example>

        <p><code>format.relative</code> says how far a time is from <code>now</code>, in the
            largest unit it fills: <code>3 hours ago</code>, <code>yesterday</code>,
            <code>in 2 days</code>. Pass <code>now</code> from a reactive value to have the words
            follow it, as the card does when a call is logged. Left out, it is the time of the
            call.</p>

        <p><code>format.date</code> takes a <code>Date</code>, epoch milliseconds or an ISO string,
            and writes it in UTC unless you pass a <code>timeZone</code>. A server has no visitor's
            zone to read, so a date written in the visitor's zone would change as the page
            hydrates.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th><code>style</code></th><th>It reads</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>'day'</code>, the default</td><td>Nov 18, 2026</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>'monthDay'</code></td><td>Nov 18</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>'month'</code></td><td>Nov 2026</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>'time'</code></td><td>3:04 PM</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>'dateTime'</code></td><td>Nov 18, 2026, 3:04 PM</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p><code>format.duration</code> writes a length of time in milliseconds in its two largest
            units: <code>1h 5m</code>, <code>1d 1h</code>, <code>45s</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
